{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>It shall be for you a perpetual statute.</b> This service." "<b>In the seventh month, on the tenth of the month, you shall afflict yourselves.</b> After Scripture says ותתענג בדשן נפשכם (Isaiah 55:2), we know that עינוי is the opposite of תענוג, and it is the fast. Furthermore, ונפש נענה תשביע (Isaiah 58:10, 11), its meaning is like ותפק לרעב נפשך (Isaiah 32:6), for it is the way of the prophets to repeat. Since we have a tradition, there is no need to search. And עניתי בצום נפשי (Psalm 35:13) is not proof because of the remembrance of a fast. The general principle: every עינוי found in Scripture joined with נפש is the fast." "<b>The native and the stranger who sojourns among you.</b> He is not exempt from doing work, nor is he cut off from the fast."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:31.254490669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}